// Notification delivery with retry and DLQ (flowchart-diagram)
// Source: notification-service/SYSTEM_DESIGN.md

title Notification Delivery

Record [shape: oval, label: "Kafka record on notifications"]
Parse [shape: diamond, label: "JSON parses?"]
Discard [shape: oval, label: "log + discard - a poison record must not stall the partition"]
FanOut [label: "for each channel in message.channels"]
Claim [shape: diamond, label: "Redis SETNX claim notif:idem:{tenant}:{id}:{channel}:{attempt}"]
Skip [shape: oval, label: "skip - redelivery already handled"]
Row [label: "load or create notifications row, attempts++"]
Template [shape: diamond, label: "template found for (tenant, name, channel)?"]
Render [shape: diamond, label: "every {{variable}} resolved?"]
Sender [shape: diamond, label: "ChannelSender registered for channel?"]
Send [label: "sender.send(...) - SMTP / FCM / SMS"]
Result [shape: diamond, label: "SendResult"]
Sent [shape: oval, label: "status SENT + providerMessageId"]
Retry [shape: oval, label: "status RETRYING - republish to notifications_retry"]
Dlq [shape: oval, label: "status FAILED - publish to notifications_dlq"]

Record > Parse
Parse > Discard: no
Parse > FanOut: yes
FanOut > Claim
Claim > Skip: already held
Claim > Row: claimed, or Redis down - fail open
Row > Template
Template > Dlq: missing - PERMANENT
Template > Render: found
Render > Dlq: unresolved - PERMANENT
Render > Sender: rendered
Sender > Dlq: none - PERMANENT
Sender > Send: found
Send > Result
Result > Sent: success
Result > Retry: TRANSIENT
Result > Dlq: PERMANENT or EXHAUSTED_RETRIES
